              "type": "lab-richtext",
              "settings": {
                "title": "Why to Test for SVHC?",
                "content": "<p>The SGS REACH SVHC Screening is an independent laboratory test that analyzes products for the presence of chemicals classified by the European Chemicals Agency (ECHA) as Substances of Very High Concern (SVHCs).</p><p>CastlePack was screened for 253 officially listed SVHCs plus one additional potential SVHC, covering many commonly discussed chemical groups such as PFAS-related compounds, phthalates, lead, and BPA-related substances. The laboratory found <strong>no tested SVHCs above the reporting threshold of 0.1% by weight</strong>, resulting in a PASS.</p>",
